# Landing-page sample diet PDF

**Not a committed static file.** The sample on the landing page is rendered live from a real program created via questionnaire + Stripe.

**Download URL (unchanged for users):**

```
https://program-creator-3tzd.onrender.com/api/samples/sample-diet
```

**Inline preview (landing embed):** same URL with `?inline=1`

## Point Render at your sample program

After you complete questionnaire + checkout with the program you want to showcase:

```bash
curl -X POST https://program-creator-3tzd.onrender.com/api/admin/public-sample-diet \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "x-contacts-admin-key: $CONTACTS_ADMIN_KEY" \
  -d '{"email":"you@example.com","programId":"<uuid>"}'
```

Or set Render env vars: `SAMPLE_DIET_EMAIL`, `SAMPLE_DIET_PROGRAM_ID`.

Config is stored on the Render disk at `public-sample-diet.json` (next to `programs.db`) so you can swap programs without redeploying.

## Code paths

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Live sample config + render | `server/publicSampleDiet.js` |
| API route | `GET /api/samples/sample-diet` |
| Admin set sample | `POST /api/admin/public-sample-diet` |
| PDF payload (same as purchased) | `js/sampleDietPrintoutData.js` → `buildSampleDietPrintoutPayload(pkg)` |
| Purchased PDF | `GET /api/programs/diet-pdf` |
| Landing page embed | `index.html` → API URLs |

## Do not

- Commit `docs/samples/b&bsamplediet.pdf` — removed; sample is live.
- Run `npm run render:sample-diet-preview` expecting a repo PDF — script only prints setup instructions.
- Confuse the landing sample with `buildSampleDietPreviewPayload()` / golden fixtures — those are for local verify only.

## Verify locally

```
npm run verify:printout-calcs
npm run verify:pdf
```
